    at the session-mean w 0.1668    +0.086172
    identity                      +0.00e+00   PASS

  CLAUSE 4's SIX BRANCHES, exercised on synthetic input before any real
  row reaches them. E = 0.0241 (the projected CLEAN SE), A = +0.1209.
    S -0.0600  A +0.1209  -> ARTEFACT DOMINATES                 ok  (below -2E)
    S +0.0100  A +0.1209  -> §53's NULL SURVIVES               ok  (inside +-2E)
    S +0.0600  A +0.1209  -> PARTIAL                            ok  (above 2E, below A-2E)
    S +0.1209  A +0.1209  -> EXPRESSES AS AVERAGING PREDICTS    ok  (within 2E of A)
    S +0.2000  A +0.1209  -> OVER-EXPRESSES                     ok  (above A+2E)
    S +0.0600  A +0.0723  -> UNDEFINED -- the models are closer than 4 SE ok  (A < 4E: the gate must REFUSE, not pick)
    branches reachable  6/6  PASS

  *** AIBABY_SLOTWIN_FORCE_GATES is set and the budget is SHORT. The
  budget-bound gates below are being read against 900k constants on a
  450000-tick run, so clauses 0 and 3 SHOULD fail. This is a branch
  exercise and NOT a measurement. ***

  CLAUSE 0 (FIRST) -- IDENTITY. The windowed scorer run over ALL probes
  must reproduce `cell_g`/`cell_n`, and through them §53's PUBLISHED table.
  If this fails the windowed numbers are not §53's session and NOTHING
  below is readable. The archive half is budget-bound and says so.
    reconstruction, worst over all 120 creatures   0.00e+00   PASS
    T1.RET       pooled SLOT -0.0173 +- 0.0142   §53 +0.0081 +- 0.0170   *** DIFFERS ***
    T1.RET.D     pooled SLOT -0.0802 +- 0.0241   §53 -0.0947 +- 0.0306   *** DIFFERS ***
    T1.ORACLE.D  pooled SLOT -0.0103 +- 0.0288   §53 +0.0211 +- 0.0327   *** DIFFERS ***
    T1.ORACLE    pooled SLOT +0.0827 +- 0.0506   §53 +0.1293 +- 0.0478   *** DIFFERS ***

  CLAUSE 1 -- BOOKKEEPING, PER EIGHTH. A pinned index makes the cells
  DIAGONAL, so T1.ORACLE's residual is identically zero and its slot term
  IS its gap. Arithmetic, not a result -- and a windowed scorer has to earn
  it again in every eighth. `ident` is gap - (slot + residual), worst case.
    ORACLE residual, worst eighth        0.00e+00   over 93 creature-eighths   PASS
    identity, worst creature x eighth    5.55e-17   PASS
    and over EVERY arm and eighth        1.11e-16   over 739 creature-eighths   PASS

  CLAUSE 2 -- VACUITY, at the PRIMARY'S GRANULARITY and on the arm that is
  KNOWN to express. The question a vacuity gate must answer here is whether
  a ~17-probe window can carry a large slot term AT ALL, and only an arm
  that expresses can answer it -- the derived arm's own column could not
  (`vacuity-gate-cannot-guard-a-rejection`).

  THE THRESHOLD IS THE ARM'S OWN POOLED VALUE AND NOT A CONSTANT, and the
  450k smoke is why: an absolute 0.08 was calibrated on §53's 900k ceiling
  and read 3/8 at 450k, where the arm's OWN pooled figure is only +0.0827.
  That gate could have failed with nothing wrong (`baseprobe-gate`).
  Required: the per-eighth MEAN recovers at least half of what the pooled
  estimator sees on the same arm at the same budget, and >= 6 of 8 eighths
  are strictly positive.
    T1.ORACLE  slot +0.0687 +0.1825 +0.1400 +0.0608 +0.0152 +0.0921 +0.0686 +0.0077 
               n         12      12      12      12      12      12      10      11 
    per-eighth mean +0.0795  vs half the pooled +0.0413 (pooled +0.0827)   PASS
    eighths strictly positive   8/8   PASS

